# SABOTAGE: S14 follow-up — the operator DLQ page's OWN write-posture statement (`#dlq-posture`) is
# dropped from the render, leaving only the per-role withheld-control note behind. This is the exact
# regression the bar exists to prevent, and it is INVISIBLE to every other assertion on this surface:
# the note still explains a read-only withhold, `authorize_write/1` still refuses, and the controls
# are still offered to an admin. What is lost is the disambiguation — with the bar gone, an ADMIN
# whose queue holds no dead envelope is back to an empty action column that reads identically to a
# role that may not write (the note renders only in the second case). So this patch is aimed at the
# posture probes alone: the bar's own element (and with it the `data-can-write` /
# `data-operator-role` / dead-count copy they assert on) disappears.
#
# NOT TOUCHED, deliberately: `@write_roles`, `may_write?/1`, `authorize_write/1`, the per-row
# `:if={e.status == "dead"}` control gate, the `#dlq-readonly` note, and the footer's role
# disclosure. This removes a STATEMENT of posture, never the posture itself — `may_write?/1` and
# `authorize_write/1` still read the same assign, so the page's behaviour is unchanged and only its
# silence becomes ambiguous again.
#
# No warning is introduced (a deleted block leaves nothing unused) and the replay runs `mix test`,
# so there is no warning to confine.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/webhook_dlq_authz_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: an :operator_admin page states writes ARE offered, and names the role it read that from
# MUST_FAIL: an :operator_readonly page states writes are WITHHELD — and never implies the queue is empty
# MUST_FAIL: with NO dead envelope the page says so — the admin's blank action column is explained
# MUST_FAIL: an unresolved role is named honestly — the posture claims no role the session does not hold
